WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.820
- Hi ladies, I brought the bagels

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.655
for the book club this afternoon.

00:00:07.655 --> 00:00:08.874
- Oh, of course you did.

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.057
- Morgan, I hope you're
bringing your famous

00:00:11.057 --> 00:00:13.193
blueberry muffins for the
bake sale on Thursday.

00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:15.039
- Of course I am, but I'm
gonna do them as cranberry

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:16.757
because blueberries are out of season

00:00:16.757 --> 00:00:18.975
and I don't need pesticides
in all those kids.

00:00:18.975 --> 00:00:19.892
- Fine.

00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:21.494
So ladies, I'm looking for volunteers

00:00:21.494 --> 00:00:23.654
to bring juice boxes for
the car wash fund raiser.

00:00:23.654 --> 00:00:26.881
- Oh, I'll bring some raw
milk, chia, hempseed smoothies.

00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:28.739
Much healthier, no sugar.

00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:29.899
- Sounds disgusting.

00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:32.291
- I'm gonna transcend
that comment right now.

00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:33.812
I've been meaning to tell you guys

00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:36.355
this morning Arachnid said
he didn't wan to nurse,

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:37.620
I think he's weaning.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.001
I don't think I'm ready for it.

00:00:39.001 --> 00:00:40.720
- Isn't Arachnid in third grade?

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.614
- Yeah.

00:00:41.614 --> 00:00:42.600
- You know what though,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.273
I've done a ton of
research on breastfeeding

00:00:44.273 --> 00:00:47.651
and actually in most
countries it is totally common

00:00:47.651 --> 00:00:50.391
for moms not to wean until
six, seven years old.

00:00:50.391 --> 00:00:52.992
I'm gonna send you guys all a
link to Doctor Sear's website

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:54.838
because every parent should
read what he's has to say.

00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:56.394
- Oh god, we don't have a computer.

00:00:56.394 --> 00:00:57.938
No, we got her a typewriter.

00:00:57.938 --> 00:00:58.971
It's just really important to us

00:00:58.971 --> 00:01:01.038
that she's raised strictly authentic.

00:01:01.038 --> 00:01:02.733
Like, she's only listened to vinyl,

00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:05.577
none of that MP3 processed stuff.

00:01:05.577 --> 00:01:06.994
- I'm here, I'm here.

00:01:06.994 --> 00:01:08.106
What day is it today?

00:01:08.106 --> 00:01:08.744
(beep)

00:01:08.744 --> 00:01:10.022
Oh my god, I locked my keys in my car.

00:01:10.022 --> 00:01:11.287
I'm here, I'm here.

00:01:11.287 --> 00:01:12.865
Wait is it Tuesday?

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:13.806
Is it soccer practice?

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:14.666
No book club.

00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:16.627
Oh, was it my day to bring the bagels?

00:01:16.627 --> 00:01:18.032
- No, no I've got the bagels.

00:01:18.032 --> 00:01:19.147
- Oh thank god.

00:01:19.147 --> 00:01:20.876
- But you have something on your shirt.

00:01:20.876 --> 00:01:22.570
- Poop or chocolate, poop or chocolate?

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.518
No one knows.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.589
Chocolate.

00:01:26.589 --> 00:01:28.075
Thank god, last time it was poop.

00:01:28.075 --> 00:01:30.095
Oh, good protein though.

00:01:30.095 --> 00:01:31.129
You know what Karen,

00:01:31.129 --> 00:01:32.636
you're a real bitch for
bringing those bagels.

00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:34.495
You knew I was gonna forget 'em.

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:36.595
It's not my fault your
child can't eat gluten.

